00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.920
Starlink's secondary network architecture opens a new path for direct device connectivity without relying solely on terrestrial gateways. This is spacex daily, episode 105. Circle ID reports that Starlink is developing a parallel network layer focused on direct-to-device links. The architecture separates user-terminal traffic from broader device connectivity. This design reduces dependency on ground stations for certain use cases.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.800
devices. The approach leverages existing satellite hardware with modified beam patterns.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.380
The report details how the secondary layer can serve maritime and aviation endpoints

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:44.500
through adjusted beam management. Circle ID notes the system maintains separation between

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:51.420
high bandwidth user traffic and lower bandwidth device signals. NASA has chosen SpaceX for the

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.540
starburst gamma ray satellite launch.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.340
The mission targets high energy astrophysics observations.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.080
SpaceX will provide the Falcon 9 vehicle for the ride.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.920
